From 204474c961d2c06755597dbeff7150b290fb361c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: =?UTF-8?q?Ren=C3=A9=20Rebe?= <rene@exactco.de>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 14:56:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Restore support for 32-bit hosts
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Revert merge 38879a667f ("Remove support for 32-bit hosts") on top of
the 11.1 stable series, so that QEMU builds and runs on 32-bit hosts
such as i586/i686 and ppc32 again.

On top of the plain revert:
- give 32-bit hosts explicit tcg_gen_deposit{,_z}_i64, tcg_gen_rotri_i64
  and tcg_gen_extract2_i64 expansions, as 11.1 emits deposit and
  extract2 unconditionally and leaves lowering to the optimizer, which
  only sees 32-bit ops on such hosts
- detect TCG_TARGET_REG_BITS in the common tcg/target-reg-bits.h
- use Stat64 for the migration counters moved to migration.c and
  savevm.c, needed without 64-bit atomics
- limit ATOMIC_REG_SIZE to pointer size without CONFIG_ATOMIC64
- size insn_start by INSN_START_WORDS * 64 / TCG_TARGET_REG_BITS

64-bit guests on 32-bit hosts remain disabled, as they have been since
10.0.  Not restored: 32-bit CI jobs and containers, mips, riscv32 and
wasm32.

Signed-off-by: René Rebe <rene@exactco.de>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
